The following rules shall apply to the conduct of the business of dealing in malt beverages and wine in the city:
(1) The beverages shall not be sold or served in private rooms;
(2) The beverages shall not be sold or served behind screens, blinds, curtains or other hiding places, but only in the open where the public is admitted;
(3) The beverages shall not be sold or served to any persons in violation of any law relating to the age of such persons;
(4) No malt beverages or wine shall be dealt in at retail by the licensee except with some other business conducted in the city for which the owner pays a license tax of not less than $25.00;
(5) The place of business of the licensee and all places and rooms in connection with the place of business over which he has control shall be subject to inspection by the county, state or city officers charged with the preservation of the peace and by their deputies.
(Code 1986, § 3-24)
